From: Bogdan Mircea <mirceapetrebogdan@gmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH] wifi: rtw88: avoid aligned loads from packed USB efuse MAC

The USB MAC address resides in a packed efuse structure. ether_addr_copy()
requires alignment that this field does not guarantee; copy its six bytes
without architecture-dependent aligned loads.

Not submitted upstream.

Signed-off-by: Bogdan Mircea <mirceapetrebogdan@gmail.com>
---
--- a/drivers/net/wireless/realtek/rtw88/rtw8822b.c
+++ b/drivers/net/wireless/realtek/rtw88/rtw8822b.c
@@ -29,7 +29,8 @@
 static void rtw8822bu_efuse_parsing(struct rtw_efuse *efuse,
 				    struct rtw8822b_efuse *map)
 {
-	ether_addr_copy(efuse->addr, map->u.mac_addr);
+	/* The USB efuse field is packed and may be odd-aligned on MIPS. */
+	memcpy(efuse->addr, map->u.mac_addr, ETH_ALEN);
 }
 
 static void rtw8822bs_efuse_parsing(struct rtw_efuse *efuse,
